WEBVTT

1
00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:53.000
In this first verse of the eighth chapter

2
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.208
of the Bhagavad Gita, Arjuna
 wants explanation from Lord Krishna

3
00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:59.250
of those deep spiritual subjects

4
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.250
that were mentioned earlier.

5
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.958
He asks questions regarding Brahman,

6
00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:08.458
adhyātma, karma, adhibhūta, adhidaiva,

7
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:09.500
adhiyajña,

8
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.041
and how to remember Lord Krishna
at the time of death.

9
00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:16.791
He asks these questions.

10
00:01:21.791 --> 00:01:23.333
What is Brahma?

11
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.666
Does its meaning refer to jīvātmā

12
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:27.583
or is it paramātmā?

13
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.583
This question was disturbing Arjuna's mind,

14
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.750
therefore he asks Lord Krishna

15
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.625
this question in this context.

16
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:36.958
If we see,

17
00:01:36.958 --> 00:01:39.291
this question searches for the essence

18
00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.041
of spiritual existence and reality.

19
00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:45.375
Then Arjuna asks,

20
00:01:45.375 --> 00:01:47.375
'What is adhyātma?'

21
00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:48.875
Behind asking this question,

22
00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.416
Arjuna's curiosity was to know

23
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:52.583
whether this relates to the gross

24
00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:55.166
physical senses

25
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:57.666
or to the subtle elements

26
00:01:57.666 --> 00:02:00.208
that operate the body.

27
00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:02.250
After asking this question,

28
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.375
Arjuna asked Lord Krishna

29
00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:07.500
another question – 'What is karma?'

30
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.791
Arjuna is asking this question to understand

31
00:02:10.791 --> 00:02:12.666
whether its meaning shows

32
00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:14.833
daily life activities

33
00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.875
or duties prescribed by the Vedas.

34
00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:20.791
After this, Arjuna asks about adhibhūta

35
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:23.583
and adhidaiva.

36
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.958
He wants to know

37
00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:26.625
whether these are the powers

38
00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:28.375
that operate material elements

39
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:30.291
and deities?

40
00:02:30.291 --> 00:02:32.666
Is this contained in the Lord's

41
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:34.000
universal form?

42
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.833
And asking in the context of adhiyajña,

43
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:38.583
he wants to understand

44
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:41.791
who ultimately is worshipped in yajña –

45
00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:42.708
Indra,

46
00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:45.958
Vishnu, or some other divine being?

47
00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:48.000
And finally,

48
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Arjuna asks an extremely important question –

49
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.500
how to remember Lord Krishna

50
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.458
at the time of death?

51
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:54.500
Understanding that

52
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.583
at that moment concentrating the mind

53
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.500
is extremely difficult.

54
00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.791
Therefore, this question becomes

55
00:02:59.791 --> 00:03:01.208
an important focal point

56
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:03.833
of this chapter,

57
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:06.916
because Lord Krishna is going to answer

58
00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:09.375
this question in great detail ahead!

59
00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:16.625
As the question,

60
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:19.166
so the curiosity;

61
00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:22.083
and as the curiosity,

62
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:25.125
so the development!

63
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:28.708
Just as waves rise in a lake

64
00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:33.625
from just one stone falling,

65
00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:35.416
similarly,

66
00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:38.166
life's deep questions

67
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:42.958
awaken waves of knowledge in the soul!

68
00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:47.333
What questions you ask in life –

69
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:51.083
this reveals the thirst for progress within you

70
00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:55.958
and the depth of understanding.

71
00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:57.208
When Arjuna

72
00:03:57.208 --> 00:04:01.208
asked Me deep questions,

73
00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:04.708
this wasn't just a display

74
00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:07.250
of scholarship,

75
00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.916
rather it was a sign of clarity of karma

76
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:17.541
and sacred search for truth within him.

77
00:04:17.541 --> 00:04:18.750
This quality

78
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:22.250
can be developed not only
 in Mahabharata's warrior,

79
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.125
but in you too.

80
00:04:26.125 --> 00:04:27.875
If you wish,

81
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:31.083
you too can become

82
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:33.791
a questioner like Arjuna.

83
00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:35.916
From how many people do you truly ask

84
00:04:35.916 --> 00:04:38.000
such questions

85
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.333
that change your life's direction?

86
00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:45.416
Entangled in your regular life-cycle,

87
00:04:45.416 --> 00:04:47.625
you mostly get trapped

88
00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:51.833
in superficial questions, like:

89
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:54.041
'What will I get from this?'

90
00:04:54.041 --> 00:04:58.166
'How can I obtain this quickly?'

91
00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:05.333
'How can I get ahead of others?'

92
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:09.791
But these questions can only
 give momentary benefit, 

93
00:05:09.791 --> 00:05:15.250
cannot change life's direction.

94
00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.000
If you learn from Arjuna,

95
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.041
then your questions will be quite different

96
00:05:23.041 --> 00:05:26.125
like

97
00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.083
'Is this duty?'

98
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:31.708
'Is this truth?'

99
00:05:31.708 --> 00:05:38.083
'What can I learn from this experience?'

100
00:05:38.083 --> 00:05:42.250
Such questions don't just bring answers,

101
00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.708
but give a vision.

102
00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:50.750
They don't just tell solutions,

103
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.875
they make paths.

104
00:05:52.875 --> 00:05:56.250
They can change not just today

105
00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.208
but the entire life's form!

106
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:03.625
Therefore, keep Arjuna-like curiosity

107
00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:06.958
in your personal life.

108
00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:09.625
Desire to know, understand,

109
00:06:09.625 --> 00:06:13.291
effort to move in the right direction.

110
00:06:13.291 --> 00:06:16.958
Don't be scared of difficult questions.

111
00:06:16.958 --> 00:06:22.166
They take into the soul's depth.

112
00:06:22.166 --> 00:06:25.166
They awaken permanent wisdom

113
00:06:25.166 --> 00:06:29.541
and decision-power within you.

114
00:06:29.541 --> 00:06:32.125
And this is that path

115
00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:36.458
which can make your
 every decision meaningful

116
00:06:36.458 --> 00:06:42.291
and every struggle purposeful!

117
00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:49.041
In the family,

118
00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.833
what questions do you ask,

119
00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:54.958
on which subjects do you discuss?

120
00:06:54.958 --> 00:06:57.791
The question is simple

121
00:06:57.791 --> 00:07:00.208
but this is the reflection

122
00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:05.166
of your values and priorities.

123
00:07:05.166 --> 00:07:09.125
The questions Arjuna asked Me

124
00:07:09.125 --> 00:07:12.500
arose not from any blind faith

125
00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:16.791
but from authentic curiosity

126
00:07:16.791 --> 00:07:20.291
that was taking him toward clarity of karma.

127
00:07:20.291 --> 00:07:21.500
This same thing applies

128
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.500
to family members too.

129
00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.416
The family's conversation determines

130
00:07:27.416 --> 00:07:30.458
what will be the future

131
00:07:30.458 --> 00:07:34.916
and karmas of children and
 youth growing up in it.

132
00:07:34.916 --> 00:07:38.333
There are also many people who believe

133
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:41.750
that spiritual discussions are boring,

134
00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.208
but this notion

135
00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:45.375
arises only

136
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:47.500
when in some home there's only talk

137
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.458
of material achievements, prestige,

138
00:07:50.458 --> 00:07:52.916
and success.

139
00:07:52.916 --> 00:07:56.125
Then subjects like soul, dharma, or karma

140
00:07:56.125 --> 00:08:00.375
naturally start seeming unfamiliar

141
00:08:00.375 --> 00:08:02.708
and boring too.

142
00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:06.000
But if these very subjects

143
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.458
are told through stories,
 experiences, self-reflection,

144
00:08:09.458 --> 00:08:13.916
and values,

145
00:08:13.916 --> 00:08:17.041
then they don't seem boring,

146
00:08:17.041 --> 00:08:19.708
they become an inspiration.

147
00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:21.291
Like

148
00:08:21.291 --> 00:08:23.333
in a family, grandmother or maternal grandmother

149
00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:26.750
tells children Ramayana's stories.

150
00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:29.666
And then children ask,

151
00:08:29.666 --> 00:08:33.041
'Why did Lord Rama accept forest exile?'

152
00:08:33.041 --> 00:08:35.458
or 'Why did Hanuman ji burn Lanka?'

153
00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:37.375
These simple questions lead toward

154
00:08:37.375 --> 00:08:40.500
deep life-values –

155
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.458
duty, truth, and justice.

156
00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:47.500
In this way, children start understanding

157
00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.500
life's deep truths through stories.

158
00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:55.958
But spirituality shouldn't be imposed on anyone.

159
00:08:55.958 --> 00:08:58.916
You can make them understand
 attentively, gently

160
00:08:58.916 --> 00:09:02.000
spirituality's importance

161
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.416
and can generate interest in them!

162
00:09:05.416 --> 00:09:10.250
In whose home's environment
 a culture of thinking deeply,

163
00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:15.166
asking questions, and
 self-contemplation is built,

164
00:09:15.166 --> 00:09:19.250
that home's children and adults
 all slowly connect

165
00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.291
with those questions

166
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:24.208
that don't just give today's answer

167
00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:30.208
but illuminate life's entire direction!

168
00:09:30.208 --> 00:09:35.375
And with time, these very discussions
 become a source of knowledge

169
00:09:35.375 --> 00:09:38.708
and enrich the family!

170
00:09:43.708 --> 00:09:45.791
What questions do you ask

171
00:09:45.791 --> 00:09:49.125
in your work field?

172
00:09:49.125 --> 00:09:56.833
This thing highlights your thinking, 
priority, and awareness.

173
00:09:56.833 --> 00:09:59.250
Like Arjuna,

174
00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.708
do you think deeply

175
00:10:00.708 --> 00:10:04.541
and lean toward subtle questions?

176
00:10:04.541 --> 00:10:09.750
Because these don't just provide
 the path of problem resolution

177
00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:14.750
but also completely resolve it.

178
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.250
Remember,

179
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.583
questions asked in the office

180
00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:24.208
determine both your future's direction

181
00:10:24.208 --> 00:10:26.666
and your development's pace!

182
00:10:26.666 --> 00:10:29.333
Listen to some superficial questions

183
00:10:29.333 --> 00:10:32.625
that people often ask,

184
00:10:32.625 --> 00:10:35.958
and along with that, know meaningful questions

185
00:10:35.958 --> 00:10:40.083
that can be asked in their place:

186
00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:43.666
A superficial question is:

187
00:10:43.666 --> 00:10:46.166
'What will I get from this?'

188
00:10:46.166 --> 00:10:49.708
Whereas a meaningful question could be:

189
00:10:49.708 --> 00:10:54.000
'What contribution can I give in this work?'

190
00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.458
Asked is:

191
00:10:56.458 --> 00:11:00.500
'How to finish this work quickly?'

192
00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.958
Whereas should be asked:

193
00:11:03.958 --> 00:11:06.375
'What benefit can our work team get

194
00:11:06.375 --> 00:11:09.791
from this work?'

195
00:11:09.791 --> 00:11:12.750
Another shallow question:

196
00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.875
'How to get promotion?'

197
00:11:15.875 --> 00:11:19.500
This question should be asked like this:

198
00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.875
'How to develop one's skills?'

199
00:11:22.875 --> 00:11:27.625
These superficial questions do
 give benefit, but momentary!

200
00:11:27.625 --> 00:11:30.208
They don't give permanent advancement.

201
00:11:30.208 --> 00:11:32.166
Whereas from these meaningful questions,

202
00:11:32.166 --> 00:11:35.666
not only does your vision become clear,

203
00:11:35.666 --> 00:11:38.750
but constancy

204
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.166
and seriousness come in your decisions.

205
00:11:41.166 --> 00:11:45.750
Ask yourself in your work field:

206
00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:52.041
'Am I only focused on targets or on purpose too?'

207
00:11:52.041 --> 00:11:55.250
'Am I building some vision for my future,

208
00:11:55.250 --> 00:12:00.875
or only carrying day-to-day burden?'

209
00:12:00.875 --> 00:12:03.875
When you ask yourself such questions

210
00:12:03.875 --> 00:12:08.125
that are connected to life values,
 purpose, and skill development,

211
00:12:08.125 --> 00:12:14.000
then your professional life doesn't remain
 only a means of economic benefit or promotion,

212
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.208
rather it becomes

213
00:12:17.208 --> 00:12:21.708
a continuous journey in which every step

214
00:12:21.708 --> 00:12:27.083
carries possibility of learning and developing.

215
00:12:27.083 --> 00:12:29.125
Arjuna's this inspiration

216
00:12:29.125 --> 00:12:31.958
isn't limited to some battlefield,

217
00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:34.916
it's equally meaningful in today's

218
00:12:34.916 --> 00:12:36.916
workplaces too!
